      "source": "frbsf.org",
      "title": "Connecting Stock Market to Labor Market During the AI Boom",
      "summary": "The artificial intelligence boom has coincided with unusually high stock valuations, echoing earlier technology-driven booms. Four economic variables can largely account for changes in the stock market’s cyclically adjusted price-earnings ratio since 1961, including most of the run-up since 2022. The most important of these is the noncyclical rate of unemployment, which points to a connection between the stock market and the labor market. This may reflect that employers value the future benefits from hiring new workers in much the same way that investors value future cash flows from stocks.",
